From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:39:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: let the J604 DCP power its display
 domains down

Make the internal display's power-down while blanked (#1059) available
on every apple_pmp_display_board(), J604 included, when its DCP node
names its PMC interface. It stays off unless appledrm.power_gate_ms is
set (default 0); say so, and that it is testing on J604, in the
parameter description.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
[j604: k610 drm sync: conflict with the !external term of the #1059 gate in 50d5865ea6 form; kept: gate_capable = !external && apple_pmp_display_board() && apple,pmc-interface.]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 3f12a7e869..4eaae15d36 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops power_gate_ms_ops = {
 
 module_param_cb(power_gate_ms, &power_gate_ms_ops, &power_gate_ms, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(power_gate_ms,
-		 "J713: power the display coprocessor and its domains down after this many ms blanked, and before system sleep (0: never, at most 600000)");
+		 "J713, J604: power the display coprocessor and its domains down after this many ms blanked, and before system sleep (0: never, the default; at most 600000; J604: testing)");
 
 /*
  * DCP CPU control and status, in the coprocessor's ASC block. The idle bit
@@ -2887,7 +2887,7 @@ int iomfb_m4_init(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 		return ret;
 	dcp->external = external;
 	/* The internal display's power-down: its PMC interface names the rest. */
-	dcp->gate_capable = !external && apple_pmp_j713_board() &&
+	dcp->gate_capable = !external && apple_pmp_display_board() &&
 			    of_property_present(dev->of_node, "apple,pmc-interface");
 	owner->v26_6 = dcp;
 	owner->rtk = dcp->rtkit;
